 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How's everything? Lots of people do, and there's no medical reason why you shouldn't. For some People working on the bed a few hours a day improves their mood. Then you' probably in the healthy extreme. What matters is that you take regular break and sit somewhere else at some point. It is, and that's the point. A lot of us find that working on the bed for an hour or two evening improves our productivity a lot. You' want take short walk or sit on a chair for an hour at least every day. Sitting all the time is bad for your back.",
